nd the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415726 1072 #uuid "a8db01df-3c54-5aa4-9e56-66901823f72a" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415726 1074 "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v‖ & \\le 2‖u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v‖ & \\le 2‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 14 & \\le 2\\cdot 3+‖v‖ \\\\ 14 & \\le 6+‖v‖ \\\\ 8 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $8.$" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415722 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415727 1069 "q-40199" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415727 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415727 1071 "If $|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖=17$ and $‖v‖=5$, then what is the smallest possible value of $‖u‖?$" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415727 1072 #uuid "af610309-e1d2-5541-8807-9bdfd83d138d" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415727 1074 "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17 & =|u\\cdot v|+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =‖u‖\\cdot (5)+‖u+v‖ \\\\  & =5‖u‖+‖u+v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the triangle inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5‖u‖+‖u+v‖ & \\le 5‖u‖+(‖u‖+‖v‖) \\\\  & =5‖u‖+(‖u‖+5) \\\\  & =6‖u‖+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two inequalities, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17 & \\le 6‖u‖+5 \\\\ 12 & \\le 6‖u‖ \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$ is $2.$" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415723 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415728 1069 "q-74107" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415728 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415728 1071 "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=5$ and $‖\\sqrt{3}u+\\sqrt{2}v‖=15.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415728 1072 #uuid "c2d432f4-839e-5c1d-a878-2fb57ff814c5" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415728 1074 "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $\\sqrt{3}u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{2}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{3}u+\\sqrt{2}v{‖}^{2} & =‖\\sqrt{3}u{‖}^{2}+‖\\sqrt{2}v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{3}u+\\sqrt{2}v{‖}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{3}‖u‖)^{2}+(\\sqrt{2}‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖\\sqrt{3}u+\\sqrt{2}v{‖}^{2} & =3‖u{‖}^{2}+2‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (15)^{2} & =3(5)^{2}+2‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 225 & =3\\cdot 25+2‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 225 & =75+2‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 150 & =2‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=5\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415729 1062 #uuid "4ee84374-5b1a-56bf-89ad-16da75d560fc" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415729 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415725 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415730 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415732 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415730 1062 #uuid "9092880c-4d43-5d7f-b7bc-995e69b8d061" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415730 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415727 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415731 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415730 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415731 1062 #uuid "a0ea2d0d-888f-5508-a231-99df6c592b2b" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415731 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134219 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415732 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415733 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415732 1062 #uuid "e9eecb7f-c678-5544-bfe8-e4de69d13094" 13194139534245 17592186045417 true] [17592186415732 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415728 13194139534245 